e vertex","+of degree 3 is the root (internal vertices have degree 4, leaves 1), that","+every internal vertex has three children and every leaf is at depth 5","+(`learning.obstruction_branch.ternary_tree_certificate`, which refuses a","+cycle, a disconnected graph and a tree with a leaf removed — the test). The","+branch lemma down the tree: at an internal vertex `v`, `S = {v}`, the three","+child subtrees are connected, pairwise disjoint and disjoint from `S`, and","+`Q = {v}` links every pair, so `pw ≥ k + 1` where `k` is a floor on every","+subtree (`branch_lemma_separator`, `lean/MOSPFormalization/Sandwich.lean`);","+the induction starts at height 1 with three single-vertex `trivial` leaves","+(`pw ≥ 0`), hence the claw `K_{1,3}` has `pw ≥ 1`, and height `h` has","+`pw ≥ h`. Written as a nested B certificate in item 06's format","+(`obstruction-branch-1`: 121 `branch` nodes, 243 `trivial` leaves, one node","+per vertex), it claims `pw ≥ 5`; the independent checker verifies it (364","+nodes checked, own BFS for every branch and connector, **0 C re-runs**,","+0.03 s). With the stored layout of width 5, **the class is closed: `pw = 5`**.","+The *value* is classical — Ellis, Sudborough & Turner (1994) compute the","+pathwidth of a tree in linear time, and the `cut-branch` recursion their","+algorithm rests on is exactly this lemma applied down the tree — so what is","+new to the record is the certificate, not the number. The C program had","+spent 236.7 core-hours on this class without a result: its search never","+sees the branch structure, and a tree of pathwidth 5 has far too many","+layouts of width 5 to refute width 4 by enumeration.","+","+**Family E on the 24** (item 02's search, `--targets open24`). The graph is","+the record's edge list; the \"witness\" is the stored layout in its *prefix*","+orientation (the dataset's own convention is the reversal; `open_class_graphs`","+checks that the prefix vertex separation equals the recorded width on all","+24, so the layout's finished sets seed `f̂(t) ≤ t + width` and the ceiling","+starts at the width); the \"optimum\" column of `ceiling.csv` is the recorded","+**width + 1**, an upper bound in optimum units, and the file says so.","+Budget `0.005 n²` s clamped to 90 s, which binds on 14 of 24 (every class","+above 266 vertices; a longer run can only lower a ceiling). The C helper","+`obstruction_expansion.c` was capped at 256 vertices (`MAXW 4`, a 256-entry","+counter) and refused these graphs; its cap is now 768 vertices (`MAXW 12`),","+checked against the exact profile on a 12-vertex graph and on the","+712-vertex class before the rerun (the first launch's three completed rows,","+at ≤ 256 vertices, were kept).","+","+**Family M on the 23** (item 04's search, `--stage open`). Every minor in a","+window of **30–85% of the vertices** (the item's rule; the evaluator skips","+anything outside it before any C call, 9,383 candidates skipped that way,","+and never a minor above 90%); the greedy ladder, both rules at 30–85% in 5%","+steps (24 points), then the tabu search from the ladder's evaluator for the","+rest of **one shared 900 s budget per class** (the item's \"20 minutes\" with","+the ladder and the search sharing it, not 20 minutes each: the ladder","+alone costs up to 24 × 20 s); the C program at **20 s per call** with its","+minor step off; the \"optimum\" the search aims at is the recorded width (a","+floor meeting it closes the class; the search cannot exceed it, since the","+stored layout bounds the pathwidth above). The upper bound that decides","+whether a candidate is sent to the C program is the recorded layout lifted","+to the minor (the cubic greedy layout is off above 150 vertices). 4 workers","+for 5,400 s wall, with the E and B runs beside it (8 processes in all; the","+one-minute load stayed at 4–7).","+","+**Family B on the 23** (item 06's search, `--stage open`). 240 s per class,","+the C program at 20 s per branch, **no branch above 90% of the vertices