ch lemma on the tree), the best new floor and its family.","+`tables.md` carries the full table with the ladder's floor, the potential","+of B, and the checker column; `joined.csv` every column.","+","+### 7.3 What the numbers say","+","+- **Two classes are closed.** `pwc-15933` (`BalancedTree_3_5`) by the","+  branch lemma, `pw = 5`. **`pwc-17632` (`NY_13`, PACE 2017 bonus, 283","+  vertices, 448 edges, recorded width 10, recorded floor 9) by family M**:","+  the search found an **85-vertex contraction minor** (173 edges, 198","+  contractions, `minor_sha256 fd5a9a10…`) that the C program proves to have","+  pathwidth 10 by refuting width 9 in **67,455 nodes and 0.07 s**, against","+  the C program's 236.7 core-hours on the whole graph with no result; the","+  stored layout has width 10, so **`pw(NY_13) = 10`**. The certificate is","+  verified by the checker on all three checks, including the rule-free one,","+  so it rests on no search rule: `pathwidth_gt_of_minorOf` (`Minor.lean`)","+  and the `checkF` family. This is the one class on which the **search beat","+  the greedy ladder** (the ladder's best, 9, is the record's floor): at the","+  same 30% rung the ladder's two rules build minors of pathwidth 9, and the","+  search's moves (1,589 C calls, 341,209 moves, 9 improvements) reached one","+  of pathwidth 10. The item's kill criterion (\"zero new floors on the 23 is","+  a verdict\") is therefore **not met**, by one class.","+- **On the other 22 the three families agree with each other and stop one","+  below the width.** Family M's floor is `width − 1` on **21 of 22** (and","+  `width − 2` on `494_bus`), always a `refutation` on a minor at the 30%","+  rung (20 of 23) or at 37–39% (3: `ex099`, `ex093`, `FLA_14`); the C","+  re-proof gives each minor's pathwidth *exactly* `width − 1`, so those","+  minors cannot certify more, and no minor in the window reached `width`","+  within the budget. So on 21 classes **the pathwidth is `width − 1` or","+  `width`**: the recorded width is at most one above the truth, and the","+  duality gap of family M is at most 1 there. The gap is not zero on the","+  evidence: the search found no closing minor, and a search's failure is","+  not a proof of absence (the budget binds on every class: 900.0 s).","+- **Five floors rise above the record, four without closing**","+  (`lower_bounds.csv`): `fuzix_vfscanf` 2 → 7 (width 8), `bcspwr05` 3 → 9","+  (10), `494_bus` 2 → 8 (10), `ex073` 3 → 9 (10) — the four classes whose","+  recorded floor was the C program's own cheap bound on a graph with a","+  low-degree fringe — and `NY_13` 9 → 10. On the other 18 the record","+  already stood at `width − 1` (MMD+ on the whole graph), and M reproduces","+  it on a minor a third of the size.","+- **Harper cannot close any of the 24, under any computation**: the ceiling","+  is **below the recorded width on all 24** (by 1 on the tree, 2 on 13, 3 on","+  8, 4 on `ex157`, 5 on `FLA_14`); only on the tree does the ceiling reach","+  `width − 1` (4, while `pw = 5`). On the tree this is the structural","+  verdict of the bounds section in `CLAUDE.md` made exact: the expansion","+  family provably misses the pathwidth of a tree with branching, and the","+  branch lemma is what sees it. The empty-pair ceiling is lower still (4–9).","+  The search found a set below the witness's prefix at 89.8% of the levels;","+  `t*` sits at 0.12–0.57 `n`. A ceiling is valid whatever the search's","+  quality (a found set only proves `f(t) ≤ b`), so this statement does not","+  depend on the budget.","+- **Family B sees only fringes.** Values 2–5 (3 on 17 classes; 5 on","+  `FLA_14`, branches `[194, 38, 30]` of widths `[10, 4, 4]`) against widths","+  7–11; above the recorded floor on 2 (`fuzix_vfscanf` and `494_bus`, both","+  2 → 3), never above M; the potential (a ceiling at the separators tried)","+  is 3–6, so the leaves are essentially exact and the shortfall is the","+  third-largest branch: every best separator isolates one large component","+  (0.86 `n` on `contiki_shell`) with two small ones, or three small","+  components once the large one is barred. Item 06's verdict (\"branching is","+  closed\") holds here, with the tree as the one structure where it is the","+  whole answer.","+- **Compute** ≈ **7.1 core-hours** of the item's 10: M 5.75 (23 × 900 s; of","+  which 5.59 in 7,839 C calls — the ladder's 366 calls 0.59, the search's","+  7,473 calls 5.0), E 0.50, B 0.39, checks 0.42 (the B leaves' re-runs at","+  100 s) + 0.002 (M) + 0.001 (rule-free), smoke runs 0.06.","+","+### 7.4 The evidence rows, and the proposal (plan §0.4 (3))","+","+`results_obstruction.csv` has the two closing rows in","+`run_unlimited.py`'s `FIELDS`, in the representative's labels (the","+representative computed as `paper1.dataset.fold` does, from the values on","+record before the fold; its graph matches the record edge for edge on all","+24, checked by `open_class_graphs`), `order` the stored witness in the","+dataset's orientation (`layout_width` = width, checked): `pwc-17632` with","+`proof=minor` and the certificate JSON in `minor` (`refuted 9, size 85,","+rule search`, the contractions, the C's node count; `dataset_check.py`'s","+own `replay_contractions` replays it to 85 vertices), and `pwc-15933` with","+`proof=theorem` and the B certificate's path, theorem and value in `minor`","+— **which `fold` does not read**: `PROOF_PROV` knows `refutation`, `minor`","+and `bound`, so a `theorem` row folds as a `solution` of the recorded width","+and is skipped. `lower_bounds.csv` has the four non-closing floors with","+their certificates and verdicts.","+","+The exact diff is `open_runs_proposal.diff`: the `OPEN_RUNS` line adding","+this file, `theorem` in `PROOF_PROV` (with the checker's item 7 extended to","+the branch-lemma case), and a `lower` field on `solution` rows carried from","+the run files' `lower` column, which every run writes and nothing consumes.","+**The `OPEN_RUNS` line is not applied**: with the `NY_13` row in the list,","+`fold` would produce a new `certified:minor` record, which is a dataset","+rebuild, and the item forbids one (`paper1.dataset run`/`write` were not","+run; `paper1/dataset.py` is untouched). Applying it is one line once the","+owner decides to rebuild.","+","+### 7.5 Kill verdict, and what this does not claim","+","+**Kill verdict: not met.** One of the 23 (`NY_13`) has a new floor that","+meets its recorded width; the planner's expectation that the 24 are \"open","+for a reason the families can see\" holds on the other 22, where all three","+families stop at `width − 1` or below and the expansion family's ceiling is","+below the width on every one. No stop condition fired: no floor is above a","+recorded width (the test asserts it), no certificate was rejected.","+","+Harness: the open classes have no certified optimum, so","+`learning/bound_harness.py`'s validity stage (\"above optimum\" must be 0)","+cannot be run on them; its stand-ins are the stored layouts (every floor","+is at most the width, checked) and the checker's 47 verdicts.","+","+**Does not claim**: that any class other than the tree and `NY_13` is","+closed; that a floor of `width − 1` makes the recorded width likely (the","+width is an upper bound and nothing here refutes anything; on 21 classes","+the truth is `width − 1` or `width` and this item cannot say which); that","+the tree's value is new (it is not; the certificate is); that no closing","+minor exists in the window on the 22 (the search ran 900 s per class and","+its moves are local); that the M floor is attainable only by search (on 22","+of 23 the greedy ladder reaches the same floor in a tenth of the time);","+that the E ceilings are the family's exact values (they are upper bounds on","+`max_t (f(t) − t)`, and the budget bound on 14 classes); that the 85-vertex","+minor of `NY_13` is minimal."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/obstruction_search.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NbbbRd6Pdy35niN4zmoC6m","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
